Ushuffle version 0.02
=====================

A Perl interface to uShuffle, a library for shuffling sequences while
preserving their k-let counts (Jiang, Anderson, Gillespie and Mayne, BMC
Bioinformatics 9:192, 2008). Such shuffles are the usual null model when
assessing the significance of a feature of a biological sequence.

    use Ushuffle qw(shuffle set_seed);

    # one shuffle that keeps all dinucleotide counts of the input
    my $shuffled = shuffle('ACACGUAGAUGGGGA', 2);

    # many shuffles of the same sequence
    my $shuffler = Ushuffle::Shuffler->new('ACACGUAGAUGGGGA', 2);
    print $shuffler->shuffle, "\n" for 1 .. 100;

    # reproducible output
    set_seed(42);

After installation, "perldoc Ushuffle" and "perldoc Ushuffle::Shuffler"
show the full documentation.

INSTALLATION

To install this module type the following:

   perl Makefile.PL
   make
   make test
   make install

DEPENDENCIES

Perl 5.10.1 or later, a C compiler, and a C library providing random() and
srandom(). No Perl modules outside the core are needed.

BUNDLED LIBRARY

ushufflelib/ contains ushuffle.c and ushuffle.h from
https://github.com/s-will/ushuffle (v1.2.2 plus the hash overflow fix of
pull request #1), unmodified.

SUPPORT

Please report bugs through the issue tracker at
https://github.com/mtw/ushuffle-perl/issues

